From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: keep bit packing with its crypto consumer

The crypto library calls dsd_unpack_bytes_to_bits, but its implementation
is only compiled into core, which already depends on crypto. Shared-library
consumers such as the AES/OFB and ECDSA tests consequently fail to link.
Compile this dependency-free utility into crypto instead. Core already
links crypto publicly, so all existing consumers retain the implementation
without introducing a circular shared-library dependency or dropping tests.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/core/CMakeLists.txt b/src/core/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/core/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/core/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -24,7 +24,6 @@ target_sources(
         time/dsd_time.c
         time/dsd_time_state.c
         util/dsd_misc.c
-        util/bit_packing.c
         util/dsd_init.c
         util/dsd_events.c
         util/call_state.c
diff --git a/src/crypto/CMakeLists.txt b/src/crypto/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/crypto/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/crypto/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ add_library(dsd-neo_crypto)
 target_sources(
     dsd-neo_crypto
     PRIVATE
+        ../core/util/bit_packing.c
         crypt-aes.c
         crypt-csi72.c
         crypt-des.c
